'' --diagnostics-file: a command-line error reaches the file, location-less, and the
'' 'end' record carries the command-line exit code.
''
'' DiagOut.Start runs before the command-line check, because Parse reads the whole line
'' whatever it finds -- so the path is known even when another argument is bad. The whole
'' file is asserted: a location-less record is an empty file field and four zeros.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --diagnostics-file build/.diagfile-cmdline.tsv -q tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: error TKO0100: unknown option '-q'
'' EXPECT-FILE-HAS: build/.diagfile-cmdline.tsv :: tiko-diagnostics\t1\nerror\tTKO0100\t\t0\t0\t0\t0\tunknown option '-q'\nend\t1\t0\t2\n
